<main><p class="kicker">LEGAL · LAST UPDATED 29 OCTOBER 2026</p><h1>Company Privacy Policy</h1><p class="intro">This policy explains how Ligos handles personal information when you visit ligos.io, use app.ligos.io, or connect services through our MCP gateway.</p>
<h2>1. Who is responsible</h2><p>Ligos is operated by Individual Entrepreneur Pavel Georgievich Stoyanov (ИП Стоянов Павел Георгиевич), Russia. Taxpayer identification number (INN): 771888304488. State registration number (OGRNIP): 326774600164773.</p><p>For privacy questions and requests, contact <a href="https://t.me/pavel_stoyanov">@pavel_stoyanov on Telegram</a>. Please identify your Ligos account, but do not send passwords, API keys or access tokens.</p>
<h2>2. Information we process</h2><ul><li><strong>Account and service information:</strong> email address, account identifiers, selected AI client, connected service settings and subscription or payment status.</li><li><strong>Connection credentials:</strong> API keys, OAuth tokens and other credentials needed to access services you choose to connect.</li><li><strong>Connected service data:</strong> information retrieved to fulfil requests, such as orders, inventory, CRM records, messages, emails and other data made available by the connected service and your permissions. This can include personal information about you or other people.</li><li><strong>Support information:</strong> messages and information you provide when asking for help.</li><li><strong>Technical information:</strong> IP address, browser and device information, request and error metadata, visited pages, referral sources and interactions.</li></ul>
<h2>3. Why we process information</h2><p>We process information to create and maintain accounts, authenticate connections, retrieve requested data, deliver results to your selected AI client, administer subscriptions and referrals, provide support, troubleshoot problems, protect the service and understand website usage.</p><p>Depending on the activity and applicable law, processing is based on providing the service you request, your consent, compliance with legal obligations, or legitimate interests in operating and protecting the service. Where consent is the basis, you may withdraw it by contacting us; this does not affect processing that has already taken place.</p>
<h2>4. Connected services and AI providers</h2><p>Ligos acts as an intermediary between services you connect and the AI client you choose. Our servers process requests and service responses to deliver this functionality. Data returned through a connection is made available to your selected AI client, for example ChatGPT or Claude. The AI provider's own terms, privacy policy, settings and retention practices apply to information it receives.</p><p>Connect only accounts you are authorised to use and ensure you have an appropriate basis for processing information about other people. Access is limited by the permissions and API capabilities of each connected service. If you use Ligos for an organisation, that organisation is responsible for determining the purposes for which its connected business data is used.</p>
<h2>5. Who receives information</h2><p>Information may be processed by hosting and infrastructure providers needed to operate Ligos, connected service providers, your selected AI provider, payment providers when you pay, and support or analytics providers where used. Information may also be disclosed where required by law or necessary to investigate abuse and protect legal rights.</p><p>External providers may process information in different countries. The location and handling of data depend on the providers and services you choose. You can contact us for information about the providers involved in your use of Ligos.</p>
<h2>6. Cookies and website analytics</h2><p>The website uses Yandex Metrica, provided by Yandex LLC, to measure visits and interactions. The counter loads when pages are visited. Analytics can involve cookies, IP addresses, browser and device details, pages viewed, referral sources and interaction or session-recording information. See <a href="https://yandex.com/legal/confidential/">Yandex's Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p>A referral cookie stores an invitation code for 60 days; a UTM cookie stores first-visit campaign information for 30 days. These help attribute registrations. You can control cookies and tracking through your browser settings and tracking-blocking tools. Blocking analytics does not prevent the main website from functioning.</p>
<h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2><p>Retention depends on the type of information and the purpose for which it is processed. Account and connection information is needed while the account or connection remains active. Support and technical records are retained for resolving requests, operating and protecting the service. Transaction records may need to be retained to meet accounting and other legal obligations.</p><p>You may request account closure and deletion of associated personal information by contacting us. We will assess the request, verify your identity where necessary and explain any information that must be retained and why. Copies already received by an external service or AI provider are governed by that provider's retention and deletion procedures.</p>
<h2 id="security">8. Security and control</h2><p>Connection credentials are stored in encrypted form. Ligos uses HTTPS for its public website and service endpoints. These measures reduce risk but do not make any online service completely risk-free.</p><p>You can disconnect a service in Ligos or revoke its API key or authorisation at the source. Revocation stops future access through that credential; it does not automatically remove information already delivered to your AI provider.</p>
<h2>9. Your privacy choices and rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law, you may request access to your personal information, correction or deletion, restriction of processing, or a copy of eligible data, and you may object to processing or withdraw consent where relevant. Contact <a href="https://t.me/pavel_stoyanov">@pavel_stoyanov</a> to make a request. You may also raise a concern with the competent data protection authority.</p>
<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy as the service and its processing activities change. The latest version will be published at this URL with its update date.</p>
